   "text": {
    "L1": "A point marks an exact position. It has no size.",
    "L2": "A line segment has two endpoints and a fixed length you can measure.",
    "L3": "A line has no endpoints and continues forever in both directions.",
    "L4": "Drawing it longer on paper does not make a different line; paper shows only part.",
    "L5": "A ray has one endpoint and continues forever in one direction.",
    "L6": "Ray AB starts at A and passes through B, so ray BA points the other way.",
    "L7": "In our example, both rays start at O: ray OA and ray OB. They point in opposite directions, so they are different rays.",
    "L8": "Which figure has one endpoint and continues in one direction? Tap it."
   },
